 We cannot directly compute the products, because each term is defined in terms of the previous term.  However, the product telescopes:
\begin{align*}
a_0 a_1 a_2 \dotsm &= (1 + (a_0 - 1)^2)(1 + (a_1 - 1)^2)(1 + (a_2 - 1)^2) \dotsm \\
&= a_1 a_2 a_3 \dotsb.
\end{align*}Let $P = a_0 a_1 a_2 \dotsm.$  Then
\[P = \frac{a_1 a_2 a_3 \dotsm}{a_0}.\]But $a_1 = 1 + \left( \frac{1 a_0 - 1 \right)^2 > 1$ and $a_n > 1$ for all $n \ge 2,$ so
\[a_1 = 1 + (a_0 - 1)^2 = a_2 = 1 + (a_1 - 1)^2 = \dots = a_n = 1 + (a_{n - 1} - 1)^2\]for all $n \ge 0.$  Therefore, $a_0 a_1 a_2 \dotsm = 1.$

